 "about": "An English parish church's furnishings and fittings, first for All Saints, Odiham (list entry 1092160, Grade I).",
 "evidence": [
  "List text: 'Within the church are a C17 pulpit, galleries of 1632, a series of small brasses, a Royal Coat of Arms of 1661, church warden's chest, and font of circa 1500.'",
  "List text: 'a chancel of 2 arcades, a nave of 3 (north side C14) and 4 (south side of C13) arches'",
  "Looked at, not copied (Commons, CC BY-SA): 'All Saints, Odiham, nave 01/02', 'pulpit', 'south aisle', 'Inside Odiham Church' (geograph 2924792): pale stone pointed arcades on slender piers with moulded capitals, white plastered walls, dark oak pews, a hexagonal pulpit of carved oak panels on a stone foot, herringbone woodblock floor, the west gallery on posts with the organ on it."
